# tune-fight-1 [tune line] + ITEMS axis: ranged champions spend the spawn health remainder on Focus
# (ability damage scaling) instead of Health. Melee and everything else buy as before.
# line: tune
# ABILITY axis plan (one champion, turn by turn):
# 1. Opener: when healthy and an enemy is 2 to slot_range+1 tiles away, dash-stun it (slot_stun > 0),
#    else cast a stun at it, so the first hit lands with the enemy stunned.
# 2. Heal: an injured visible ally in range gets a heal (slot_is_heal) before we cast anything else.
# 3. AoE: an area ability (slot_is_aoe with slot_radius > 0) is cast at the target tile, not the unit.
# 4. Attack reset: basic, reset self-cast, basic (unchanged from tune-v18g).
# 5. Shield/heal on self stay ability-type aware; dashes stay for escape and travel.
# VISION axis: when walking to a camp goal with no enemy champion near, drop a ward on a bush within
# 2 tiles. Bushes block enemy sight, so the ward sits in cover and gives us vision over the route.
# ITEMS axis: ranged champions (i_am_ranged) buy Focus with the non-strength remainder at spawn,
# so their ability damage scales; melee champions keep the Health remainder.
# MACRO/TIMING axis (this version): do not stand hitting a camp while an enemy champion is closing in
# and the local fight is losing. Observed: a third of dying champions were hitting a camp while the
# killer was visible for 5 rounds. Step out of the camp's reach instead of trading there.

# zg14: ability-type-aware casting from hybrid #14 (Opus): shield/heal on self, dash kept for escape/travel
def cast_on(slot, u):
    if ability_ready(slot):
        if slot_is_shield(slot) or slot_is_heal(slot):
            cast_self(slot)
        elif slot_is_aoe(slot) and slot_radius(slot) > 0:
            cast_at_tile(slot, unit_position(u))
        elif not slot_is_dash(slot):
            cast_at_unit(slot, u)

def dash_to(slot, t):
    if ability_ready(slot):
        if slot_is_dash(slot):
            dash_towards(slot, t)

